family jig-client-wire 19
# Accounts.accounts/signing, AccountLine.sources and Account.sources: jig_client_domain::Limits::document_bytes; each item is a length-prefixed piece
# AccountLine.uses and Account.uses: jig_domain_accounts::USES (16)
# OutcomeAccountSignInStarted.address: jig_domain_people::ADDRESS (2048 bytes).
# TaskPage.live and EndedRows.rows: jig_client_domain::Limits::document_bytes
# Me.projects and MeProject.templates: jig_client_domain::Limits::document_bytes
# Envelopes carry the owner version; each end checks its served range.
# Text fields and path/pattern item bytes: jig_client_domain::Limits::text.
# Page rows, window rows and lists without an independent count: jig_client_domain::Limits::rows.
# Resource path and authority pattern segment counts: jig_client_domain::Limits::segments.
# Authority entries and amendment implications: jig_client_domain::Limits::authority.
# Owned documents, nested length-prefixed pieces and recursive fact tables: jig_client_domain::Limits::document_bytes.
# Create.tasks: jig_client_domain::Limits::document_bytes, capped at 1048576 bytes.
# Charter.instructions: jig_client_domain::Limits::document_bytes, capped at 1114240 bytes.
# Settings request pieces: jig_client_domain::Limits::ask_bytes, capped at 1114240 bytes.
# Charter.alternatives, PolicyEditTemplates.overrides, SettingModel.efforts and SettingPolicy.templates: jig_client_domain::Limits::rows, capped at 16.
# ModelSetNames.names and SettingModel.name: jig_client_domain::Limits::text, capped at 4096 bytes.
# SettingModel.program, effort and efforts item bytes: jig_client_domain::Limits::text, capped at 32 bytes.
# SettingsDocument.settings: jig_client_domain::Limits::document_bytes, capped at 256 settings.
# Account/source/sign-in item counts: jig_client_domain::Limits::accounts; their pieces share document_bytes.
# Recursive fact parents precede children; indexes share one ordered table whose first row names the root.
# Reads keep the engine's cursor opaque (protocol/client/README.md, section 4).
# Unreachable is a local connection outcome; the engine sends no such record.
# Nested collections are length-prefixed pieces; their owner splits and admits them.
# Task and run documents (client/domain/contract/documents.md and client/domain/contract/README.md, 5.3).
# Keyed.value: a request's carried value, sent once, never stored (protocol/client/README.md, 3).
# Dependencies replace the whole list: newly named tasks are added, omitted tasks removed (domain/tasks/changes.md).
# The description's 512 bytes are MODEL_DESCRIPTION_BYTES (protocol/limits.md).
# The task's next-run wait, with source deadlines already translated to wall time.
# Shared admission vocabulary precedes the task wait that reuses it.
# Remaining documents and stream (protocol/client/wire.md, 1, and protocol/client/README.md, 5).
# Account deadlines are optional wall times; absence supplies no deadline.
# Account changes share the account documents' payer type and ACCOUNT_USES bound.
# Small store (protocol/client/README.md, 7); TableEntry.request has Keyed.request's ceiling.
# A read value preserves the contract variant as well as its existing document.
# Chips.rows and Inbox.needs/updates/selection: jig_client_domain::Limits::document_bytes; each item is a length-prefixed piece.
# A delivery preserves its contract variant and the whole document.
# Settings and revision history (protocol/client/wire.md, section 1).
